    "Logging Levels\n",
    "The standard library has five built-in logging levels in increasing order of severity: \n",
    "\n",
    "    DEBUG (10): Detailed information for diagnosing problems.\n",
    "    INFO (20): Confirmation that things are working as expected.\n",
    "    WARNING (30): Indication that something unexpected happened or might happen in the future. This is the default effective level.\n",
    "    ERROR (40): A serious problem that prevents a function from running.\n",
    "    CRITICAL (50): A severe error that might cause the program to stop running. \n"
